			"notes": "# 2.1 | CHANGELOG\n\n## ✨ ARMOR FEEDBACK\n\nArmor can now visually react when it takes damage.\n\n- Added new effects for normal armor damage;\n- Heavy durability loss now produces a stronger effect;\n- Added unique effects for fire, explosions, projectiles and fall damage;\n- Added a new effect when Mending restores armor durability;\n- Every effect can be enabled or disabled individually.\n\n## ⚙️ CUSTOMIZATION\n\n- Added Mod Menu support;\n- Added a new in-game configuration screen.\n\n## 🛡️ MOD COMPATIBILITY\n\n- Added support for Advanced Netherite armors;\n- Added support for Deeper and Darker's armors and Elytra.\n\n## 🔧 FIXES\n\n- Fixed the default leather armor icon color on newer Minecraft versions.\n\n## 📦 VERSION SUPPORT\n\nFuture updates will be available for:\n\n- Minecraft 1.20.1;\n- Minecraft 1.21.1;\n- Minecraft 1.21.11;\n- Minecraft 26.1.2;\n- Minecraft 26.2.\n\nSupport has ended for Minecraft 1.21.2–1.21.10, 26.1 and 26.1.1."
		}
